
  <sn><md>### `//` Delimited Comments

**Version:** ≥ C99

C99 introduced the use of C++-style single-line comments. This type of comment starts with two forward slashes and runs to the end of a line:

```c
// range of comment \n
// this is my comment
```

This type of comment *does not support multi-line* content directly. However, you can create a comment block by placing several single-line comments consecutively:

```c
// each of these lines are a single-line comment
// note how each must start with
// the double forward-slash
```

Single-line comments may be placed on their own line or at the end of a line of code. However, because they terminate at the end of the line, they **cannot** be used in the middle of a code line.

**Example usage:**

```c
// this comment is on its own line
if (x &amp;&amp; y) { // this comment is at the end of a line
    // this comment is within an if, on its own line
}
```</md></sn>
